.TH AVR\-TOKEN 1 "" "avr 0.4.1" "Avrea CLI"
.SH NAME
avr-token \- Create and manage scoped access tokens.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B avr token
[OPTIONS] COMMAND [ARGS]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Create and manage scoped access tokens.
.PP
A scoped access token is a credential bound to one organization that expires within seven days. It reaches only the repositories and VMs it names, and it cannot create further tokens. To use one, set AVR_TOKEN to the credential and AVR_ORG to the organization ID.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
create
Create a scoped token and print its credential.
.TP
list
List live tokens, newest first.
.TP
revoke
Revoke a token.
.TP
view
Show a token's details and grants, including a revoked or expired one.
